  "term": "fastigial nucleus",
  "definition": "The fastigial nucleus is a structure in the cerebellum. In the supplied source, stimulating it electrically is described as reducing brain infarction size and supporting recovery of neurological function after cerebral ischemia, although the exact protective mechanism is unclear.",
